## 4. Auth

**Standard:** Feature specs use the `setup` project + `storageState: playwright/.auth/user.json`; opt out only when the scenario is login or unauthenticated access; use API/session injection for bulk or manual scripts when UI login is too slow.

✅ **Good** (`tests/auth.setup.ts` + unauthenticated opt-out in `tests/ds2-display-program.spec.ts`):

```typescript
// auth.setup.ts — runs once, saves session
await new LoginPage(page).signIn(email, password);
await page.context().storageState({ path: authFile });
```

```typescript
test.describe('unauthenticated', () => {
  test.use({ storageState: { cookies: [], origins: [] } });
  test('cannot open edit without session', async ({ page }) => {
    await new ProgramsPage(page).goto();
    await expect(page).toHaveURL(/\/login/);
  });
});
```

❌ **Bad:**

```typescript
test.beforeEach(async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/login');
  await page.getByLabel('Email').fill(process.env.DIDAXIS_EMAIL!);
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Sign In' }).click();
});
```

**Why:** Per-test UI login adds minutes to the suite and flakes on network; stored session matches how real users stay signed in.

