## 5. Test data

**Standard:** Every created record gets a unique name (`uniqueSuffix(testInfo.testId)` or equivalent); import `test` from `fixtures/cleanup.fixture.ts` and register programs with `trackProgram` / `trackProgramCreatesFromResponses` so teardown DELETE runs automatically.

✅ **Good** (`tests/ds5-filter-program.spec.ts` + `fixtures/test-data.ts`):

```typescript
import { test, trackProgramCreatesFromResponses, captureApiTokenFromPage } from '../fixtures/cleanup.fixture';
import { uniqueSuffix } from '../fixtures/test-data';

test.beforeEach(async ({ page, trackProgram, apiToken }) => {
  captureApiTokenFromPage(page, apiToken);
  trackProgramCreatesFromResponses(page, trackProgram);
});

test('filter by name', async ({ page }, testInfo) => {
  const suffix = uniqueSuffix(testInfo.testId);
  const name = `Web Development 2026 ${suffix}`;
  // ... create via POM, IDs tracked for DELETE after test
});
```

❌ **Bad:**

```typescript
import { test } from '@playwright/test';

test('creates program', async ({ page }) => {
  await createProgram(page, 'Web Development 2026'); // static name, no cleanup
});
```

**Why:** Parallel runs collide on fixed names and leave junk data that breaks filters, empty-state tests, and quotas.

