## 8. Accessibility

**Standard:** Key surfaces (always Programs; new pages/modals per `a11y-checks`) get an axe scan with `wcag2a` / `wcag2aa` tags plus a keyboard path axe cannot cover; drive UI via POMs; never `.disableRules()` to go green.

✅ **Good** (`tests/programs.a11y.spec.ts` + `fixtures/a11y-expect.ts`):

```typescript
test('Programs page meets WCAG 2 A/AA (axe)', { tag: '@regression' }, async ({ page }) => {
  await expectNoAxeViolations(page);
});

test('Keyboard opens New Program dialog', { tag: '@regression' }, async ({ page }) => {
  const programs = new ProgramsPage(page);
  await programs.tabUntilNewProgramButtonFocused();
  await expect(programs.newProgramButton).toBeFocused();
  await programs.pressEnter();
  await expect(programs.newProgramModal.dialog).toBeVisible();
});
```

❌ **Bad:**

```typescript
const results = await new AxeBuilder({ page }).disableRules(['color-contrast']).analyze();
expect(results.violations.length).toBeLessThan(5);
await page.click('text=New Program');
```

**Why:** Silencing rules hides real WCAG defects; keyboard coverage catches focus traps and non-button activations axe misses.

