## 9. Assertions

**Standard:** Default to auto-retrying web-first `expect(locator)`; use `expect.soft` for multiple independent checks in one test; use `toHaveScreenshot` only when the UI is stable and functional asserts cannot express the regression.

✅ **Good** (web-first — `tests/ds5-filter-program.spec.ts`):

```typescript
await expect(programs.rowText(row, program.name, true)).toBeVisible();
await expect(programs.rowText(row, program.description)).toBeVisible();
```

✅ **Good** (*advised — use for validation matrices e.g. DS-3; not in repo yet*):

```typescript
await expect.soft(modal.programName).toHaveAccessibleDescription(/required/i);
await expect.soft(modal.createButton).toBeDisabled();
await expect(test.info().errors).toHaveLength(0);
```

❌ **Bad:**

```typescript
const text = await row.textContent();
expect(text).toContain(name);
await expect(page).toHaveScreenshot(); // on live programs list with changing rows
```

**Why:** Soft asserts surface all validation failures in one run; snapshotting volatile lists produces false reds; DOM reads skip Playwright’s retry window.

---

## 10. Anti-flake

**Standard:** Local `retries: 0`, CI `retries: 2` (never above 2); `fullyParallel: true` — no `workers: 1` to green a run; pinned `locale` / `timezoneId` in config; freeze time with `page.clock.install()` for relative dates; isolate mocks per test (`unroute` / fresh `page`).

✅ **Good** (`playwright.config.ts` + relative-time pattern):

```typescript
// playwright.config.ts — do not override in specs
fullyParallel: true,
retries: process.env.CI ? 2 : 0,
use: { locale: 'en-CA', timezoneId: 'America/Toronto', trace: 'on-first-retry' },
```

✅ **Good** (*advised — use when asserting “2 hours ago”; no spec in repo yet*):

```typescript
test('relative last updated', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.clock.install({ time: new Date('2026-06-15T14:30:00') });
  const programs = new ProgramsPage(page);
  await programs.goto();
  await expect(programs.lastUpdatedFor('Web Development 2026')).toHaveText('2 hours ago');
});
```

❌ **Bad:**

```typescript
test.describe.configure({ retries: 3 });
test('dates', async ({ page }) => {
  await programs.goto();
  await expect(programs.lastUpdatedCell).toHaveText(formatRelative(new Date()));
});
```

**Why:** Extra retries and serial workers mask product bugs; live clocks make relative-time asserts non-deterministic across machines and CI.

