## Do / Don't quick reference

| Do | Don't |
|----|--------|
| Locators via role → label → text → test id in POM constructors | CSS, XPath, `.first()` on ambiguous lists |
| `await expect(locator).toBeVisible()` / `.toHaveText()` | `waitForTimeout`, `expect(await …isVisible())` |
| Specs assert; POMs click/fill/goto | `expect` inside `pages/` |
| Rely on `setup` + `storageState`; opt out for login/auth tests | UI login in every `beforeEach` |
| `uniqueSuffix(testInfo.testId)` + cleanup fixture `trackProgram` | Static program names; manual `afterAll` DELETE |
| `request` for API contracts and manual scripts | Hardcoded JWTs in repo |
| `page.route` / `fulfill` / `abort` for error and empty states (recon copy first) | Mock the API call whose success you assert |
| Axe `wcag2a`/`wcag2aa` + keyboard via POMs on key pages | `.disableRules()` or invented a11y shortcuts |
| Web-first expects; `expect.soft` for multi-field validation | One-shot DOM reads; drive-by screenshots on live data |
| Trust `playwright.config.ts` retries/locale/TZ; `page.clock` for relative time | `workers: 1`, retries > 2, or `new Date()` in relative asserts |

---

## Refusals (hard stops)

When asked to do any of the following, **stop and raise the conflict** — do not comply, soften, or work around:

- **Weaken or delete an assertion to pass** — refuse. Green via a loosened or removed `expect` is a bug; escalate.
- **Heal a failure triage classified as a real bug** — refuse. Route to bug-reporter; self-heal is for locator drift only.
- **Replace a role-based locator with CSS/XPath** — refuse. Re-discover via role + accessible name, or escalate if none exists.
- **Use `waitForTimeout`** — refuse. Use web-first `expect(locator)` instead.
- **Hardcode a credential** — refuse. Use env / `storageState` / project secrets only.
- **Use the `any` type** — refuse. Type the value properly or escalate the typing gap.
